{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-r-linear-category","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-r-linear-category","kind":"remark","title":"$R$-linear category","tags":["glossary","category-theory","enrichment"],"defines":["r-linear-category"],"text":"glossary-r-linear-category.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-r-linear-category\"></a><p><strong><dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-r-linear-category\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear category</dfn>.</strong> A category whose hom-sets carry the structure of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-modules (for a commutative ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>) such that composition is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-bilinear.</p>\n<p><strong>Mathlib reference.</strong>\n<code>CategoryTheory.Linear R</code> (class).\nImport: <code>Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/glossary/glossary-r-linear-category.md","heading":"Remark","number":"24.4.1"}
